flowchart TD
    App["Application send()<br/><b>does:</b> copies intent into a socket syscall<br/><b>why next:</b> kernel must turn bytes into protocol data<br/><b>state:</b> user buffer + socket fd"]
    Sock["socket send path<br/><b>does:</b> resolves fd to struct socket/sk and calls proto sendmsg<br/><b>why next:</b> TCP owns SOCK_STREAM byte semantics<br/><b>state:</b> locked sock and msg iterator"]
    Queue["tcp_sendmsg_locked<br/><b>does:</b> copies bytes into skbs on write queue<br/><b>why next:</b> push policy/window says data may be transmitted<br/><b>state:</b> queued skbs with sequence numbers"]
    Xmit["tcp_write_xmit<br/><b>does:</b> applies cwnd, rwnd, pacing, and SACK/loss state<br/><b>why next:</b> selected skb is allowed on the wire<br/><b>state:</b> skb chosen and TCP header fields ready"]
    TCPHdr["tcp_transmit_skb<br/><b>does:</b> finalizes TCP header/checksum metadata<br/><b>why next:</b> IP must route an L4 packet<br/><b>state:</b> skb contains TCP segment"]
    Route["ip_queue_xmit / route<br/><b>does:</b> finds dst, source address, MTU, gateway<br/><b>why next:</b> output path needs dst->output and nexthop<br/><b>state:</b> skb_dst points at rtable"]
    LocalOut["LOCAL_OUT + POST_ROUTING<br/><b>does:</b> applies local policy, conntrack/NAT, mangle<br/><b>why next:</b> accepted skb can leave IP stack<br/><b>state:</b> marks/NAT/checksums may be changed"]
    Neigh["neighbour output<br/><b>does:</b> resolves L2 destination (ARP/ND) and builds L2 header<br/><b>why next:</b> device queue needs a complete frame<br/><b>state:</b> skb has output device and L2 header"]
    DevQ["dev_queue_xmit<br/><b>does:</b> runs tcx/tc egress and chooses qdisc path<br/><b>why next:</b> packet must be scheduled against device queue<br/><b>state:</b> skb may be marked, dropped, redirected, or enqueued"]
    Qdisc["qdisc / __qdisc_run<br/><b>does:</b> shapes, orders, and dequeues packets<br/><b>why next:</b> driver ring has transmit budget<br/><b>state:</b> skb handed to driver start_xmit"]
    Driver["ndo_start_xmit<br/><b>does:</b> maps skb data for DMA and fills TX descriptors<br/><b>why next:</b> NIC owns descriptors after doorbell<br/><b>state:</b> bytes are pending hardware transmit"]
    Wire["NIC / wire<br/><b>does:</b> transmits frame and later completes descriptors<br/><b>state:</b> skb can be freed after TX completion"]

    App --> Sock --> Queue --> Xmit --> TCPHdr --> Route --> LocalOut --> Neigh --> DevQ --> Qdisc --> Driver --> Wire

    classDef us fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb
    classDef tcp fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706
    classDef ip fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a
    classDef dev fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#6366f1
    classDef hw fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626
    class App,Sock us
    class Queue,Xmit,TCPHdr tcp
    class Route,LocalOut,Neigh ip
    class DevQ,Qdisc,Driver dev
    class Wire hw
